<title>USA: U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</title>
<headline>U.S. mortgage application volume fell in latest wk.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The volume of U.S. mortgage applications fell 9.9 percent in the week ended November 15, according to a Mortgage Bankers Association of America weekly survey.</p>
<p>Specifically, the volume of applications to refinance mortgages fell 4.0 percent in the latest survey week, while applications to purchase mortgages fell 12.4 percent.</p>
<p>The seasonally adjusted refinancing index climbed 6.7 percent to 445.7 from 417.9 the previous week, it said.</p>
<p>The purchase index rose 1.1 percent to 196.3 in the latest survey from 194.2 the previous week, it said.  </p>
